__pycache__/
*.pyc
main.py
.venv/
.DS_Store

# Raw inputs live on storage and are not distributed with the repository; processed
# data is regenerable from them. Seven exceptions are tracked, none of them a
# pipeline output and all of them things the repo cannot function without: the
# site shapefile, the constraint observations, the converted initial condition
# ensemble, the site labels, the site covariates, the Natural Earth archives
# the map basemap is built from, and the NEE tower table. The constraint files
# are held in the repository rather than symlinked because the upstream copies
# are edited and moved in place; see data/raw/constraints/provenance.md.
data/raw/*
!data/raw/sites/
!data/raw/constraints/
!data/raw/initial_conditions/
!data/raw/site_labels/
!data/raw/covariates/
!data/raw/natural_earth/
!data/raw/net_ecosystem_exchange/
# Un-ignoring the directory un-ignores everything in it; the inputs that
# still live on storage and are symlinked in are excluded again here. The
# initial conditions are tracked as one converted file; PEcAn's 800,000-file
# source tree it was made from is the SCC-only files/ symlink.
data/raw/constraints/nee
data/raw/constraints/sda_8k_site_rdata
data/raw/initial_conditions/files
# The NEE tower table, the reanalysis's tower list and the provenance record
# are tracked; the converted time series (about a gigabyte), the link to the
# AmeriFlux download and AmeriFlux's site listing, which carries contact
# details, are not.
data/raw/net_ecosystem_exchange/*.nc
data/raw/net_ecosystem_exchange/*.nc.partial
data/raw/net_ecosystem_exchange/fluxnet
data/raw/net_ecosystem_exchange/ameri_sites.tsv
data/processed/

.claude/worktrees/
